2. Additional English tasks
Pronunciation: Practise word stress, sentence stress, connected speech and difficult sounds.
Conversation: Role-play situations such as shopping, travelling, interviews and meeting new people.
Idioms and expressions: Learn natural phrases used by fluent English speakers.
Spelling and punctuation: Practise spelling, capital letters, commas and full stops.
Translation: Translate short sentences from your first language into English.
Comprehension: Answer questions about texts, recordings and videos.
Critical thinking: Explain your opinions, compare ideas and give reasons.
Fluency: Speak and write without translating every sentence in your head.






