1. Vocabulary — words and meanings
Purpose: To understand people and express your ideas.
Learn everyday words, verbs, adjectives, phrases, synonyms, antonyms, and phrasal verbs.
Example: happy, improve, difficult, look after.
2. Grammar — rules of English
Purpose: To make correct and meaningful sentences.
Learn parts of speech, sentence structure, tenses, articles, prepositions, conjunctions, and conditionals.
Example: She works every day. She is working now.
3. Listening
Purpose: To understand spoken English.
Practise conversations, different accents, questions, instructions, and natural speech.
4. Speaking
Purpose: To communicate confidently with others.
Practise sentence formation, asking questions, answering, conversations, storytelling, and expressing opinions.
5. Pronunciation
Purpose: To speak clearly and understand how words sound.
Learn individual sounds, word stress, sentence stress, rhythm, and connected speech.
6. Reading
Purpose: To understand written English and build vocabulary.
Read messages, stories, articles, instructions, and longer texts.
7. Writing
Purpose: To communicate clearly in written form.
Practise sentences, paragraphs, emails, messages, descriptions, and formal writing.


